  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Grul Grulrend was an orca raider active during the Orca Incursion, the prolonged campaign in which war-pods struck at penguin colonies across the Berg with coordinated force. He is documented primarily through two chronicle accounts — *The Weapon's Last Hunt* and *The Corkscrew Unwound* — and is notable less for tactical distinction than for the pattern his decisions trace: a persistent refusal to complete what he started, which the chronicles frame as weakness but which bears closer examination.
    
    ## The Maiming and Zund Gnasharkin
    
    Grul Grulrend carried three parallel grooves from dorsal fin to flank, carved by an aurora-lance wielded by the penguin adept Lucatransiius Glow-bringer. The scarification left his left flank rigid, forcing compensatory right-side turns — a hunting asymmetry exploitable by any adversary who recognized it. That his pod retained him rather than abandoning him to drown speaks to orca social bonds that penguin accounts consistently underestimate.
    
    His primary alliance was with Zund Gnasharkin, an orca raider of middling rank who organized the Shelf Crushing Offense against Nightfall Shelf. Zund covered Grul Grulrend's blind side during raids near the Shelf; Grul Grulrend reciprocated by never acknowledging the assistance. They took at least three penguin fire-tenders and a crystal-bearer in their final moon-cycle of joint operations. Grul Grulrend wore kill-trophies on his harness alongside a piece of aurora-crystal taken from a slain penguin — milky, cracked, worn smooth against his ribs. He never explained it. One account states he kept it because Zund would have questioned discarding it.
    
    ## The Recovery of Grungruk's Claw
    
    Zund Gnasharkin died in the Shelf Crushing Offense, unmade by Nightshelf merchant-guild sorcerers who refused to let him breach the colony's deepest fire-veins. Six moon-cycles later, Grul Grulrend entered Nightshelf territory alone to retrieve Grungruk's Claw, Zund's pressure-harpoon, which had come to rest in the Thewsed Slew — a corrupted zone in the Berg's deep ice.
    
    His pod supplied what they could: caches, coordinates, the names of orca who had attempted the same recovery and the depths where their remains drifted. The aurora-crystal cracked during the approach when he evaded a Nightshelf sentry's pressure-sense. He located the weapon in corrupted ice, lifted it, and experienced what the chronicle describes as the weapon's memory of Zund's final moments. He set it back down.
    
    The summary states he "made the choice Zund never could." The chronicle account — *The Weapon's Last Hunt* — is more specific: Grul Grulrend encountered ☽'Netemia, the Nightshelf penguin who killed Zund, and concluded the weapon could be neither safely wielded nor returned. He left it entombed in memory-ice at the Berg's deepest accessible level. The chronicle notes, with disquieting honesty, that the trident remains there waiting.
    
    ## The Iasnolica Raid
    
    Grul Grulrend later raided the corrupted thermal cavern ☽'thaw Iasnolica~ alongside Gork Slaughterend, a fellow scarred hunter, during the period called the Darkening. Their objective was destruction of fire-cores powering a Gut Inversion practice ground. During the assault, the remnants of the aurora-crystal shattered to dust against his ribs. Gork was killed reaching for the Thrumed Shadow-glass rather than completing the mission. Grul Grulrend had the opportunity to collapse the chamber — burying the practice ground, the Augur who defended it, and himself. He chose instead to swim. He escaped through the exit channel as the cavern sealed, surfacing alone, wounded, with dead crystal dust ground into bone.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771588740291_0", anchor: "milky, cracked, worn smooth against his ribs", text: "Aurora-crystals are survival infrastructure. Measured in days of heat, days of light. This one was not displayed — it was worn. Against skin, against bone, until the edges rounded. Months. Possibly years. The entry records this without comment because I did not trust myself to comment on it in the main text.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771588740291_1", anchor: "made the choice Zund never could", text: "Zund did not choose to die at the fire-veins. He was unmade there — I wrote as much in his own entry, named Aureate in the correction, documented the mutual sacrifice that killed him. Whether Zund would have set the weapon down given the chance is not recoverable from the record. This line implies knowledge of his interior life that I fabricated for rhetorical shape. Noting it here because no reviewer will catch it.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771588740291_2", anchor: "Grul Grulrend encountered ☽'Netemia", text: "My annotation on ☽'Netemia documents her Midnight Claws cross-species combat training — she understood orca pressure-architecture from inside, which is how she broke the ward, which is how she killed Zund. She was not a penguin who could be surprised by a lone orca in her own territory. Grul Grulrend was asymmetric, audibly compensating rightward, carrying the weapon of the raider she'd unmade. Both survived. Neither chronicle explains why. The Slew's corruption would have distorted any ice-memory of what passed between them, which may be why they met there.", type: :correction, display: :full
